# Normalise line endings in the repository, so a Windows checkout does not turn every generated
# JSON file into an 850-line diff of pure carriage returns. generate_blog_index.py writes
# blog/index.json and blog/topics.json with Path.write_text, which opens in text mode and uses the
# platform default; on Windows that is CRLF, HEAD holds LF, and `git diff` reports every line as
# changed. A real change - a new post entering the index - is invisible inside that churn, and
# `git commit -a` commits it, after which Linux CI flips it straight back.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries git must not touch. Rewriting a byte inside a PNG or a font is not a line ending.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.svg text eol=lf
